+---
+"@agent-wechat/cli": patch
+---
+
+Keep authenticated native quote responses encrypted before parsing them and bind each response to its original account, send and payload. Reopen retained responses after a restart without sending again. Stop accepting file-shaped success replies as quote receipts: native quote success remains `needs_review` until the supported Linux response schema has independent evidence. Preserve explicit service rejections and keep simulator results separate from native wire evidence.
diff --git a/docs/src/content/docs/how-it-works/sends.mdx b/docs/src/content/docs/how-it-works/sends.mdx
--- a/docs/src/content/docs/how-it-works/sends.mdx
+++ b/docs/src/content/docs/how-it-works/sends.mdx
@@ -41,6 +41,7 @@
 Stopping the daemon (or disconnecting) doesn't log you out. Only `wx auth logout` does, and after that the daemon won't reconnect on its own until you log in again.
 
 <Aside title="Good to know">
+- **Native quoted replies still need response validation.** A success-shaped reply currently stays `needs_review` with `quote_receipt_schema_unverified`. Its encrypted response is kept for inspection and can be reopened after a restart without sending again. This is not a confirmed rejection; keep the original key.
 - **Voice longer than 60 seconds is split** into equal notes. A partial result keeps the IDs of the notes that went out.
 - **Closing the connection doesn't cancel anything.** Ctrl-C on the CLI or a dropped HTTP request leaves the daemon's work running.
 - **Media writeback repair:** if a sent or downloaded file didn't make it into the profile's own folders, `wx jobs repair-writeback` finishes the job from files the daemon already has. It never downloads or sends anything.
